## HUD font glyphs: hud_char_j / hud_char_q / hud_char_v / hud_char_x / hud_char_z

Files:
  textures/segment2/segment2.hud_char_j_custom.rgba16.png
  textures/segment2/segment2.hud_char_q_custom.rgba16.png
  textures/segment2/segment2.hud_char_v_custom.rgba16.png
  textures/segment2/segment2.hud_char_x_custom.rgba16.png
  textures/segment2/segment2.hud_char_z_custom.rgba16.png

Source:   HackerSM64 (https://github.com/HackerN64/HackerSM64), v2.0.0
Author:   thecozies
Added:    2021-12-30 (HackerSM64 commit f3e61a31)

These five 16x16 rgba16 glyphs are original community-drawn art that fills
the null J/Q/V/X/Z slots left by the vanilla US (and CN) HUD font -- they
are NOT extracted from any Nintendo ROM, and are used here specifically to
avoid the Nintendo-IP JP-ROM-ripped alternative. HackerSM64 ships no
LICENSE file; this NOTICE records the provenance and attributes the
original artist and source project, per HackerSM64's own stated intent as
a base for romhacks. If you are the artist/maintainers and want a
different attribution or removal, please open an issue.

Wired into the null `main_hud_lut` slots in bin/segment2.c (spec #75,
sub-issue #77): src/game/hud.c's render_hud_top_right_corner uses the
existing print_text HUD font path, and these glyphs are what make names
containing J/Q/V/X/Z render as real letters instead of garbage.

## Red-coin HUD glyph: red_coin

File:
  textures/segment2/segment2.hud_char_red_coin_custom.rgba16.png

Source:   HackerSM64 (https://github.com/HackerN64/HackerSM64), v2.0.0
Author:   thecozies
Added:    2021-12-30 (HackerSM64 commit f3e61a31)

This 16x16 rgba16 glyph is original community-drawn art matching the shape
of the vanilla GLYPH_COIN glyph, recolored red -- it is NOT extracted from
any Nintendo ROM (no region ships a red-coin HUD glyph in vanilla SM64),
and is used here specifically to avoid inventing a JP-ROM-ripped
alternative. HackerSM64 ships no LICENSE file; this NOTICE records the
provenance and attributes the original artist and source project, per
HackerSM64's own stated intent as a base for romhacks. If you are the
artist/maintainers and want a different attribution or removal, please
open an issue.

Wired into the null US/CN `main_hud_lut` slot 54 (GLYPH_RED_COIN, the slot
GLYPH_PERIOD/texture_hud_char_decimal_point occupies on JP/SH) in
bin/segment2.c (spec #75, sub-issue #78): src/game/hud.c's
render_hud_top_right_corner draws it as the in-level red-coin readout's
marker glyph, shown once gRedCoinsCollected >= 1.
